From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:40:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] BaseTools: No debug directory in the PE images of a release
 build

GenFw leaves the debug directory of each module in its PE image, with
the CodeView entry that names the .dll it was made from by the absolute
path of the build: the same sources gave a different payload in every
directory (116 such paths in the payload of ouroBIOS), and a build is
reproducible only from the same path. --zero, which GenFw has for this,
drops the directory for the release builds; the debug builds keep it,
where the loader names the modules in its messages from it.

---
diff --git a/BaseTools/Conf/tools_def.template b/BaseTools/Conf/tools_def.template
index 72ca0dfa2..79b701ca3 100644
--- a/BaseTools/Conf/tools_def.template
+++ b/BaseTools/Conf/tools_def.template
@@ -1502,6 +1502,10 @@ RELEASE_XCODE5_X64_CC_FLAGS   = -target x86_64-pc-win32-macho -c    -Os       -W
 ##################
 *_*_*_GENFW_PATH                   = GenFw
 *_*_*_GENFW_FLAGS                  =
+# A release build with no debug directory in its PE images: the CodeView
+# entry names the .dll of the module with the absolute path of the build,
+# so the same sources gave a different image in every directory.
+RELEASE_GCC_*_GENFW_FLAGS          = --zero
 
 ##################
 # Asl Compiler definitions
-- 
